From: EmuFive <blue0x1>
Date: 2026-11-26
Subject: [PATCH 0047] buffer cache: Garlic memory for GPU-shared chunks

Sony's GPU driver maps GPU data with non-snooped page entries (Garlic);
only Onion memory snoops the CPU caches. With KYTY_GARLIC_MEMORY=1, GPU-shared
chunks the game fully allocated with a Garlic type (KYTY_GARLIC_TYPES, default 3)
take a write-combined memory type instead of the cached one. Chunks holding
command buffers stay cached; images in Garlic chunks upload by GPU copy. Each
guest memory type is logged the first time a chunk of it moves.
---
